(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// Frames and threads (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4; PYS7 (a)): a frame is a heap object holding a code"] [6 1 "// object's locals, cells, value stack and instruction index; the dispatch loop (eval.go) runs a"] [7 1 "// thread's frames without holding them on Go's stack, so a call from Python to Python is a new frame"] [8 1 "// and a return pops it, and a generator (PY5d) is a frame kept between resumptions."] [10 1 "// Frame is an executing code object (CPython's _PyInterpreterFrame and frame object)."] [13 21 "// the function run, nil for a module's or class's body"] [16 17 "// the namespace of a module's or class's body (a module's is its Globals)"] [17 2 "// LocalsMap is a class body's namespace when __prepare__ returned a dict subclass: the name"] [18 2 "// operations go through its __getitem__, __setitem__ and __delitem__ (CPython's STORE_NAME on a"] [19 2 "// non-exact dict), Locals its dict. Added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b: enum's"] [20 2 "// EnumDict)."] [22 21 "// the fast locals; nil is unbound"] [23 21 "// the cells, then the free variables' cells"] [25 16 "// the next instruction"] [26 16 "// the instruction running, or the last run (f_lasti; tracebacks' line)"] [28 2 "// Suspended is set by a yield (PY5d): the frame returned a value but is kept to be resumed."] [30 17 "// the loop returns when this frame returns: it was called from Go"] [31 2 "// reraisedAt and reraisedLasti: a reraise N set the frame's reported instruction back to the raise it"] [32 2 "// re-raises (RERAISE's oparg: frame->instr_ptr), while its handler is still looked up at the reraise"] [36 1 "// FrameType is the frame objects' type (sys._getframe, a traceback's tb_frame)."] [41 1 "// Line is the frame's current line (f_lineno), 0 when the code has no lines."] [44 1 "// ReportedLasti is f_lasti: Lasti, or after a reraise N there the instruction it re-raises from."] [64 1 "// popN pops n items and returns them in stack order (a view, valid until the next push)."] [75 1 "// Thread is a Python thread's state (PyThreadState): its current frame, the exception being"] [76 1 "// handled (sys.exception()), the call depth against the recursion limit. One thread runs at a time"] [77 1 "// (the GIL: PYS10 (a), PY6)."] [81 17 "// the exception being handled at this level (None outside handlers): the frame's or generator's slot"] [82 2 "// outer are the slots of the levels a running generator or coroutine was resumed from (CPython's exc_info"] [83 2 "// stack, gi_exc_state's previous_item): sys.exception() is the first that is not None (CurrentHandled)"] [86 2 "// cdepth is the C level's depth (PY7): the nested built-in calls CPython guards by _Py_EnterRecursiveCall"] [87 2 "// (comparison, repr, str, a tuple's hash, isinstance's and issubclass's recursions, the eval loop entered from"] [88 2 "// C), which CPython 3.14 measures on the machine's stack and pyi counts (enterRecursiveCall)"] [90 26 "// the containers being repr'd (Py_ReprEnter)"] [93 1 "// CurrentHandled is the exception being handled (_PyErr_GetTopmostException): this level's slot, else the"] [94 1 "// first not None of the levels it was resumed from; None when none is."] [107 1 "// chainContext is _PyErr_SetObject's implicit chaining: exc's __context__ the exception being handled, a cycle"] [108 1 "// through exc in that chain cut first."] [126 10 "// a cycle not through exc"] [136 1 "// reprEnter is Py_ReprEnter: true when o is already being repr'd (a recursive container: \"[...]\")."] [148 1 "// reprLeave is Py_ReprLeave."] [151 1 "// The C level's stack (PY7). CPython 3.14 raises RecursionError \"Stack overflow (used N kB)WHERE\" when a guarded"] [152 1 "// built-in call (_Py_EnterRecursiveCall) finds the machine's stack past its soft limit; a Python frame does not use it."] [153 1 "// pyi's built-ins recurse on Go's stack, a goroutine's at most 1 GB, which a deep enough structure overflowed (a fatal"] [154 1 "// Go error: test_tuple's test_hash_deeply_nested, test_copy's reflexive comparisons, test_isinstance's recursions)."] [155 1 "// pyi counts the guarded levels instead, and Go's calls into the machine (Thread.run: the eval loop entered from C,"] [156 1 "// where \"\"): cStackLevels of them, cFrameBytes each as the message's nominal kB (about"] [157 1 "// CPython's 1 MB soft limit on Linux); CPython's own depth varies with the call (on Alpine aarch64 a tuple's hash"] [158 1 "// reaches 10,000 levels, its repr not)."] [164 1 "// enterRecursiveCall is _Py_EnterRecursiveCall(where): false, with the RecursionError, past the limit; else the"] [165 1 "// level is entered and leaveRecursiveCall leaves it."] [178 1 "// stackOverflow is _Py_CheckRecursiveCall's RecursionError."] [183 1 "// leaveRecursiveCall is _Py_LeaveRecursiveCall for enterRecursiveCall's thread."] [192 1 "// currentThread is the running thread (the GIL's holder)."] [195 1 "// unbound is the marker :load-fast-and-clear pushes for an unbound local (PEP 709)."] [202 1 "// newFrame makes the frame of a function's call with its arguments bound (CPython's"] [203 1 "// _PyEval_MakeFrameVector); args holds the positional then the keyword arguments."] [226 1 "// bindArgs puts a call's arguments into the parameters' slots (positional, *args, keyword-only,"] [227 1 "// **kwargs, then the defaults), raising CPython's TypeErrors (Python/ceval.c's, with the qualified name)."] [342 1 "// joinNames is CPython's list of names: 'a', 'a' and 'b', 'a', 'b', and 'c'."] [367 1 "// newGeneratorHook makes the generator, coroutine or async generator object of a call's frame (its"] [368 1 "// code flagged :generator or :coroutine): PY5d's gen.go sets it."] [371 1 "// callFunction calls a Python function from Go: a frame run by a nested loop to its return."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[68 12] [68 30] [99 27] [99 35] [100 21] [208 47] [258 21] [258 43] [270 15] [270 30] [281 26] [295 19] [295 41] [312 28] [312 41] [319 12] [319 25] [328 18] [328 40]]} (go/file "frame.go" :imports [

